<title>USA: U.S. Spring/White Wheat - Spring wheat bids weaker.</title>
<headline>U.S. Spring/White Wheat - Spring wheat bids weaker.</headline>
<dateline>CHICAGO 1996-09-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>Dark northern spring wheat cash bids remained weaker on Thursday, prompting many producers to store their stocks in bins and wait for stronger prices, dealers said.</p>
<p>December MGE spring wheat futures slumped 2-3/4 cents to end at $4.34-1/4 a bushel.</p>
<p>&quot;It is very quiet,&quot; a Minnesota dealer said. &quot;Farmers are hanging on, waiting for the market to go up.&quot;</p>
<p>North Dakota farmers are finishing off harvesting. &quot;There is no movement,&quot; another dealer said.</p>
<p>In Montana, more rain is needed for farmers to prepare their winter wheat seedings, dealers said.  </p>
